docs/src/user/en\controller.md:3:On Retail and WoW: Forever, WowVision can be played with a gamepad next to the keyboard. Both work at the same time, and every WowVision binding can have controller buttons as well as keys. This page explains how to switch it on, what every button does, and how to change the buttons.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:14:WowVision then answers the controller in its windows and in the world. Several things only appear while Enable Gamepad UI is on: the controller buttons in the keybinding window, the four gamepad bars in the action bars window, and the controller log.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:31:While a WowVision window is open, WowVision takes the D-pad and the face buttons. These are the defaults. The names in the first column are the binding names shown in the keybinding window.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:38:| Close (Escape) | B. Where Escape belongs to the game, B runs the game's own Escape instead; this is the Close (Controller) binding. |
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:91:The window is headed "Main Menu, Page 2 of 3", for example; the wheel has three pages and the emote wheel has none. A slice that the game shows greyed out is read with ", Disabled", and one that is currently open with ", opened". An empty slice is read as "Empty". The slice for the buffs is not supported yet and says "Not supported yet" when you press it.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:124:Every binding lists its controller buttons in the keybinding window, but only while the gamepad interface is on.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:126:1. Open the WowVision menu (Shift+F1, or both shoulders and A), then UI, then Bindings.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:127:2. Move to the binding you want. Its row holds its keys first, then Add (for a key), then its controller buttons, then Add Controller Button.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:129:4. To add one, activate Add Controller Button. You hear the binding's name and "Press a controller button". Hold the shoulders, triggers or right stick press you want to combine, and press the button. As you press, WowVision speaks the combination, for example "Left trigger + A button". The button is taken when you let go of it.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:131:6. If the button already belongs to another binding, you are asked "This input conflicts with ...  Replace?". Confirm to take it from the other binding.
docs/src/user/en\controller.md:133:The capture gives up and says "Cancelled" if you press Escape on the keyboard, if ten seconds pass without a press, or if combat starts. In combat it does not open at all and says "Not in combat". See [Keybindings](./basics/keybindings.md) for the rest of the keybinding window.
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:16:| Text to speech | TTS Alert | Speaks text with your TTS voice, for example "combat started". |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:19:| Beacon | Beacon Sound | A directional sound that tells you where a waypoint is. Only used by navigation. |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:23:Example: Zone Changed Alert has a TTS Alert (on) and a Sound Alert (off). Out of the box, you hear the zone's name. If you want a chime as well, switch on the Sound Alert. If you only want the chime, switch off the TTS Alert too.
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:45:| Message | TTS | Only on TTS outputs that take their text from elsewhere, such as Announce Errors and the TTS Alert of a monitor rule. Alerts with wording of their own (combat started, a zone name, a chat message and so on) do not have it. When you type text here, it is spoken every time instead of the usual text. Leave it empty to hear the usual text. |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:48:| Beacon Sound | Beacon | A browser like the sound browser, for the beacon sounds. Moving onto one plays a sample. |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:54:3. Down to TTS Alert, Enter, then Down (past Priority Message (interrupts)) to Voice, Enter.
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:60:2. Open Speak Compass Direction. Open Voice Alert and turn Enabled off. Go back and open TTS Alert, turn Enabled on.
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:78:| Speak Compass Direction | Navigation, Compass | The direction you face changes (north, northeast, east and so on). | Voice Alert (on; recorded directions), TTS Alert (off) |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:89:| Beacon | Navigation, Maps | A route or beacon is active. | Beacon Sound (a directional ping that speeds up as you turn towards the target), Beacon Aligned (a click when you face it), Beacon Off Course (when you turn away), Waypoint Reached (when you arrive) |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:91:Inside instances the game does not report which way you face, so Speak Compass Direction stays silent there while the other compass alerts keep working. The settings of Fall Detection (Delay (milliseconds), Ignore Jumps) are in the module's screen, see [Movement](../world/movement.md). The arrival settings of Beacon are in [Navigation](../world/navigation.md).
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:99:| Target Crowd Control | Targeting, Hard Target | Your target becomes crowd controlled by anyone (stunned, feared, polymorphed and the like), or you switch to one that is; and again when it is free, or when you switch from a crowd controlled target to a free one. Not available on The Burning Crusade Anniversary. | Controlled Sound, Free Sound, TTS Alert (off; speaks "Controlled" or "Free") |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:109:| One alert for each chat tab, named as the tab is named in the game (for example General) | Chat | A message arrives on that tab. | TTS Alert (speaks the message), Sound Alert (a chat sound), and the choice Speak Messages: When the Tab Is Shown (the default) or Always |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:120:| Announce Errors | Errors | The master switch for game error and info messages ("Ability is not ready yet", "Out of range"). It also voices Lua errors and messages the filter cannot sort. | TTS Alert |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:121:| One entry for each message you have seen | Errors, Per-Error Filter | That message appears. | TTS Alert (on), Sound Alert (off) |
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:123:The Per-Error Filter lists each message with its state read after its name: "Speech", "Sound", "Speech and Sound" or "Muted". Open one to change it. The Show All Known Errors checkbox at the top lists every message the game knows, including ones you have not met yet. Repeat Delay (2 seconds, 0 to 30) stops the same error from being spoken again while you hold a key. See [Combat](../world/combat.md).
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:145:Each alert has a Sound Alert and a TTS Alert, and both outputs start off, so a new monitor is silent until you switch them on. The monitors page explains how to set them up. See [Monitors](../information/monitors.md).
docs/src/user/en\basics\alerts.md:151:- If a TTS alert is cut off too quickly by other speech, switch on Priority Message (interrupts) for it. If it keeps cutting off everything else, switch it off.
