docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:135:| Binding | What it does |
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:144:A dock is a waiting place for a ship, zeppelin or tram stop. Choosing one in F10 routes you to its waiting point on foot. When you arrive, you hear what to wait for, for example: "Dock Ship dock to Auberdine reached. Wait here for the ship. Board when you hear it arrive. The beacon shows the boarding direction; I turns you toward it." The beacon then leads to a boarding point a few yards ahead and ends there: "Boarding point Ship dock to Auberdine reached". WowNav cannot tell when the vehicle is there; you board by ear.
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:154:If you choose the portal or the tram entrance itself as your destination, you are guided to a point just before it and told: "Prepoint reached. Walk straight ahead through the entrance or portal; the beacon stays on until the activation area." Then: "In the activation area. Keep walking straight ahead; only a map change confirms the transition. The route stays on until then." After the map change you hear "Map change after the activation area; route ended. The destination is not confirmed."
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:170:If you choose one of these portals or the waiting point of the Wind Bridge itself as your destination, you hear at the prepoint "Prepoint reached. Walk on to the portal; the beacon stays on until you are there." (for the bridge "Prepoint reached. Walk on to the waiting point of the Wind Bridge; the beacon stays on until then."). At the portal you hear "At the portal. Target it with soft targeting and interact with it; the route stays on until the transition is confirmed.", at the bridge "At the waiting point of the Wind Bridge. Wait until you hear the bridge, then step into the wind current."
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:178:3. A beacon now sounds from the water, 15 yards out, in the middle of your cast range. Press I to face the water, then cast.
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:179:4. The beacon stops when you walk away from the spot (more than 20 yards), when you press Shift+F12 or when you start a new route.
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:181:The water point is only there to face. WowNav never routes you into the water. If the network ends farther from the spot than your cast range, you hear the usual "The network ends ... from the target" instead, and no beacon starts.
docs/src/user/en\world\wownav.md:196:| Step Back at Gates | On | When you drift sideways at a gate, the beacon goes back one waypoint ("One waypoint back"). |
