docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:20:The Compass module watches your character and speaks when something about your surroundings changes. Each of its entries is an alert (see [Alerts](../basics/alerts.md)): it has an Enabled switch and one or more outputs, usually TTS Alert (speech) and Sound Alert.
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:24:| Speak Compass Direction | You turn to face a different one of the eight directions | Voice Alert on, TTS Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:25:| Zone Changed Alert | You enter a new zone | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:26:| Subzone Changed Alert | You enter a new subzone (an area within a zone) | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:27:| Outdoors Alert | You go from indoors to outdoors | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:28:| Indoors Alert | You go from outdoors to indoors | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:29:| Flying Started Alert | You take off on a flying mount | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:30:| Flying Ended Alert | You land | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:31:| Swimming Alert | You enter the water | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:32:| Diving Alert | Your character goes under the surface | TTS Alert on, Sound Alert off |
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:38:By default the direction is played from a recorded voice pack (the Voice Alert output) rather than spoken by text to speech. If you prefer text to speech, turn TTS Alert on and Voice Alert off. In the Voice Alert settings you can also choose a different voice pack. See [Speech](../basics/speech.md).
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:57:2. Turn TTS Alert off.
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:135:Here is what happens: you release your spirit; WowVision looks up where your corpse is, first on your current map and then on the larger maps around it (this finds a corpse that lies in the next zone from the graveyard you woke up in), and says "Corpse". It then starts a route to it, just as if you had chosen the corpse in the navigation window. Where WowNav route data is available (WoW: Forever), a corpse that lies over several floors is routed to the lowest floor that can be reached. If no route can be found, a beacon points straight at the corpse instead. The route is followed like any other; see [Navigation](navigation.md) for how routes and the beacon sounds work.
docs/src/user/en\world\movement.md:175:- [Navigation](navigation.md): routes, waypoints, the beacon and turning to waypoints.
docs/src/user/en\windows\action-bars.md:9:| Shift+F4 | Opens the Action Bars window. Unlike most windows, it does not need a game frame to be open first. It is called Action Bars in the keybinding window and can be rebound there. |
docs/src/user/en\windows\action-bars.md:14:You cannot navigate the window while you are in combat. WowVision gives its keys back to the game during combat so that your own key bindings keep working, and takes them again when combat ends. Use your normal bindings for abilities in a fight.
docs/src/user/en\windows\action-bars.md:44:Not read: the bars that Retail added beyond the four above (Action Bars 5, 6 and 7), the extra action button, the zone ability button, and the vehicle or possess bars. Use your normal game key bindings for those.
docs/src/user/en\windows\action-bars.md:86:Using abilities is faster with your normal game key bindings. The window is for checking and rearranging your bars.
docs/src/user/en\world\scanner.md:5:Press F9 to open the Scanner. Press Escape to close it. The key is called Scanner in the keybinding window and can be changed there; see [Keybindings](../basics/keybindings.md). The Scanner works on every game version, but what it can list depends on the version and on the data available. See "Version notes" at the end.
docs/src/user/en\world\scanner.md:93:- If there is no route data, you hear "Beacon set" followed by the distance in yards, for example "Beacon set 40 yards", and a sound beacon guides you in a straight line. When you arrive you hear "Arrived".
docs/src/user/en\world\scanner.md:114:5. Press Enter. The Scanner closes and the navigation window opens, or you hear "Beacon set 40 yards" if there is no route data.
docs/src/user/en\world\scanner.md:121:3. Press Enter to be guided. Follow the beacon or the route.
docs/src/user/en\world\scanner.md:131:- Enter opens the [navigation window](navigation.md) where map data exists for the continent, and falls back to a straight beacon elsewhere.
docs/src/user/en\world\minimap.md:21:Press Ctrl+Shift+F (Scan Minimap) to scan once. The binding can be changed in the keybinding window; see [Keybindings](../basics/keybindings.md). You can also type `/wv mscan`.
docs/src/user/en\world\minimap.md:70:On the newer clients some NPCs show their title as the minimap name, for example "Skinning Trainer" instead of the person's name. When you arrive at a seen NPC by following a beacon from the Scanner, WowVision looks at the NPCs around you and, if one carries that title, says its real name followed by the name the minimap showed, for example "Olivia Burnside, Skinning Trainer". The real name is remembered for the session, and Enter on the same entry later speaks it again on arrival.
docs/src/user/en\world\minimap.md:128:| TTS Alert, Enabled | On | Speaks the name with a text to speech voice. |
docs/src/user/en\world\minimap.md:129:| TTS Alert, Voice | Game voice 0 | Which game voice speaks. It does not follow your Speech Voice setting. The first voice has the number 0. |
docs/src/user/en\windows\character.md:81:3. Once a set is selected, one stop each for Equip, Save, Edit Set and Delete. Equip puts the selected set on. Save stores what you wear now into it. Edit Set opens the name and icon window. Delete asks the game for a confirmation popup, which you answer like any [popup](system.md).
docs/src/user/en\windows\character.md:83:New Set and Edit Set open the set window as a window of its own: a name edit box, an icon type dropdown, an Icon number you change with Left and Right (it reads "3 of 120"; Enter lets you type a number) and the Okay and Cancel buttons. The window opens with the cursor in the name box cleared, so you can use the arrow keys at once; Enter on the name box puts you back into typing.
docs/src/user/en\world\quests.md:117:| TTS Alert, Enabled | On | Speaks the announcement. |
