---docs/src/user/en/controller.md:89-104---
89:- The lower row is the left half: south, south-west, west, north-west.
90:
91:The window is headed "Main Menu, Page 2 of 3", for example; the wheel has three pages and the emote wheel has none. A slice that the game shows greyed out is read with ", Disabled", and one that is currently open with ", opened". An empty slice is read as "Empty". The slice for the buffs is not supported yet and says "Not supported yet" when you press it.
92:
93:| Button | What it does |
94:|---|---|
95:| Left stick | Moves in the grid, one step at a time. While the wheel is open the stick does not walk your character. |
96:| A or Enter | Closes the wheel and runs the slice. The window it opens has the focus. |
97:| Shoulders | Turn the pages of the wheel. |
98:| D-pad and the other buttons | Stay with the game's wheel and work as they do for sighted players (the D-pad reaches sitting and the emote pages). |
99:| B or Start | Close the wheel. |
100:
101:Tracking opens the WowVision scanner and chat opens the WowVision chat window. Every other slice (social, bags, clock, PvP, the emotes) runs the game's own action.
102:
